# LyFlow Suricata global thresholds.
#
# Install into the sensor's /etc/suricata/threshold.config (the named volume
# mounted at /etc/suricata) and reload rules. This file is kept in the repo so
# the tuning survives a rebuild of the runtime image.
#
# GPL SNMP public access (sid 2101411) fires once per target when an internal
# scanner sweeps the server zone with community "public". The scan itself is
# still visible through the ET SCAN rules; keeping one alert per source per
# hour preserves that evidence without logging the whole sweep.
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2101411, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 3600
